{"seq":36,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0987"},"reason":"Added a note on the mansard's eponym: most references (Kent HER/Historic England thesaurus, Encyclopedia.com, Dictionary.com) name François Mansart, while the Duden derives Mansarde from Jules Hardouin-Mansart.","by":"provenance-research","sources":[{"url":"https://heritage.kent.gov.uk/ThesaurusTerm/137974"},{"url":"https://www.duden.de/rechtschreibung/Mansarde"}],"changes":[{"field":"notesEn","old":"","new":"Mansard: most references name the roof after François Mansart (1598–1666), who popularised it; some dictionaries, such as the Duden, derive the word from his great-nephew Jules Hardouin-Mansart instead."},{"field":"notesDe","old":"","new":"Mansarde: Die meisten Nachschlagewerke führen das Dach auf François Mansart (1598–1666) zurück, der es populär machte; manche Wörterbücher, etwa der Duden, leiten das Wort dagegen von seinem Großneffen Jules Hardouin-Mansart ab."},{"field":"notesRu","old":"","new":"Мансарда: большинство справочников связывают название крыши с Франсуа Мансаром (1598–1666), который её популяризировал; некоторые словари, например Duden, возводят слово к его внучатому племяннику Жюлю Ардуэну-Мансару."}],"hash":"96aa4c8ad10a","actor":{"kind":"agent","name":"provenance-research"},"run":"provenance-research-2026-10-23","chain":"d4909fb019482a9c0bf2dcc1f569047388402dbca5a078b2d66396d39c02b10b"},
